LS.push({id:'assign',emoji:'🔔',title:'Exercise & assignment',sub:'Including early assignment',
scenes:[
{t:'<b>Exercise</b> = the buyer <b>uses</b> the right. Exercising a <b>call</b> means buying 100 shares at the strike. Exercising a <b>put</b> means selling 100 shares at the strike.',
 a:()=>svg(newbie(110,110)+emo(300,110,'🔔',60,'pulse')+T(300,170,'"I exercise!"','#facc15',20,'popin',.4)+flyDoc(150,200,470,200,.8,1.8,'📦')+T(470,140,'100 shares','#4ade80',17,'popin',1)+T(300,280,'Call: buy at the strike  •  Put: sell at the strike','#e8ecf5',15,'popin',1.4))},
{t:'<b>Assignment</b> = a seller gets picked to fulfill the contract. The <b>Options Clearing Corporation (OCC)</b> assigns exercises to brokers, and brokers pick among their customers who are short that option (often at random).',
 a:()=>svg(`<g transform="translate(300,140)"><g class="spin" style="animation-duration:3s"><circle r="70" fill="#243056" stroke="#facc15" stroke-width="4"/>${[0,1,2,3,4,5].map(i=>`<text x="${Math.cos(i*1.047)*45}" y="${Math.sin(i*1.047)*45+8}" font-size="22" text-anchor="middle">🧑</text>`).join('')}</g></g>`+T(300,40,'Who gets assigned? 🎲','#facc15',18,'popin')+T(300,270,'Sellers of that option can be picked','#e8ecf5',16,'popin',.6))},
{t:'At expiration, the OCC <b>automatically exercises</b> equity options that are in the money by <b>$0.01 or more</b>, unless the owner tells their broker not to. Most traders simply <b>sell (close) the option before expiration</b> instead.',
 a:()=>svg(calendarIcon(130,140,'EXPIRATION','🏁')+box(260,70,300,56,'#4ade80','ITM by $0.01+ → auto-exercised','#0b1020',16,.5)+box(260,150,300,56,'#f87171','OTM → expires worthless','#fff',16,1)+T(410,250,'Tip: close before expiration','#facc15',17,'popin',1.6))},
{t:'<b>American-style</b> options (most US stock options) can be exercised <b>any day</b> before expiration, so sellers can be <b>assigned early</b>. This is most common for a <b>short call that is deep ITM right before an ex-dividend date</b>, because the buyer wants the dividend. <b>European-style</b> options (like <b>SPX</b> and <b>XSP</b>) can only be exercised <b>at expiration</b>.',
 a:()=>svg(box(40,60,250,110,'#60a5fa','🇺🇸 American: any day','#0b1020',18)+box(310,60,250,110,'#a78bfa','🇪🇺 European: only at expiration','#0b1020',16,.5)+T(165,200,'Most US stock options','#60a5fa',15,'popin',.8)+T(435,200,'SPX, XSP index options','#a78bfa',15,'popin',1)+T(300,260,'Early assignment risk → mostly American-style','#facc15',16,'popin',1.4))},
{t:'For a buyer, exercising early usually <b>throws away the remaining time value</b>. Selling the option usually gets more money. Also watch out for <b>pin risk</b>: if the stock closes very near your short strike at expiration, you may not know whether you\'ll be assigned.',
 a:()=>svg(box(60,90,220,90,'#4ade80','Sell it: $6.50','#0b1020',22)+box(320,90,220,90,'#f87171','Exercise: $5.00 value','#fff',20,.5)+T(300,230,'Example: stock $100, 95 call priced $6.50','#9fb0d0',15,'popin',1)+T(300,265,'Exercising wastes the $1.50 of time value','#facc15',17,'popin',1.4))}],
take:['Exercise = the buyer uses the right. Assignment = a seller must fulfill it.','Options ITM by $0.01+ are auto-exercised at expiration, unless you instruct otherwise.','American-style can be exercised any time, so early assignment is possible, especially before ex-dividend dates.','European-style (SPX, XSP) exercises only at expiration. Closing before expiration avoids surprises.'],
tryit:el=>{el.innerHTML=`<h3>🔔 Expiration-day simulator</h3><p>Pick a position, then slide the closing price on expiration day.</p>${seg('ap',[['lc','I own a 100 call'],['sp','I sold a 95 put'],['sc','I sold a 105 call (no shares)']],'lc')}${slider('ac','Closing stock price',85,115,.01,100.5)}<div id="ao" class="outbox"></div>${SIM}`;
 const f=()=>{const S=val('ac'),p=segVal(el,'ap');setv('ac','$'+S.toFixed(2));let h='';
  if(p==='lc'){const itm=S-100>=.01;h=itm?`✅ ITM by $${(S-100).toFixed(2)} → <b>auto-exercised</b>. You buy 100 shares at $100 = <b>$10,000</b>, which needs to be in your account. Selling the call before the close avoids that.`:`🗑️ Not ITM by $0.01 → <b>expires worthless</b>. No shares change hands.`}
  else if(p==='sp'){const itm=95-S>=.01;h=itm?`🔔 The put is ITM → you will likely be <b>assigned</b>. You must BUY 100 shares at $95 = <b>$9,500</b>, though they\'re worth $${(S*100).toLocaleString('en-US',{maximumFractionDigits:0})} now.`:`😌 The put expires worthless. You keep the premium.`}
  else{const itm=S-105>=.01;h=itm?`🔔 Assigned → you must SELL 100 shares at $105 that you don\'t own, so you\'ll be <b>short 100 shares</b> (worth $${(S*100).toLocaleString('en-US',{maximumFractionDigits:0})}). That\'s risky!`:`😌 The call expires worthless. You keep the premium.`}
  $('#ao').innerHTML=`<div class="big">${h}</div>${Math.abs(S-(p==='lc'?100:p==='sp'?95:105))<.3?'<p class="y">⚠️ Pin risk: the stock is very close to the strike, so the outcome is uncertain. Many traders close positions before the bell.</p>':''}`};bindSeg(el,f);onAll(el,f)},
quiz:[
{q:'At expiration, a stock call that is $0.05 in the money will usually be…',o:[['Automatically exercised'],['Ignored','The threshold is $0.01, so $0.05 counts.'],['Cancelled by the exchange','The exchange doesn\'t cancel it.'],['Turned into cash for stock options','Stock options settle in shares.']],a:0,ex:'The OCC auto-exercises equity options that are ITM by $0.01 or more, unless the owner instructs otherwise.'},
{q:'When is early assignment of a short call MOST likely?',o:[['When it\'s deep ITM right before an ex-dividend date'],['When it\'s far OTM','No one exercises an option that\'s worth nothing.'],['Right after you open the trade','Early assignment is uncommon except in special cases.'],['On European-style options','Those can\'t be exercised early.']],a:0,ex:'The call owner may exercise early to own the shares and collect the dividend.'},
{q:'SPX index options are…',o:[['European-style and cash-settled'],['American-style and settle in shares','That describes most stock options.'],['Never exercised','They settle at expiration.'],['Only for futures accounts','SPX options trade in securities options accounts.']],a:0,ex:'SPX (and XSP) exercise only at expiration and settle in cash.'},
{q:'You own a call with lots of time value left. Usually the better move is to…',o:[['Sell the option rather than exercise it'],['Exercise immediately','That throws away the time value.'],['Let it expire','If it\'s ITM, letting it expire leads to exercise, and it wastes the time value.'],['Call the company','The company doesn\'t handle your option.']],a:0,ex:'Selling captures both intrinsic and time value, while exercising captures only intrinsic.'}]});

